{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"72f5a91eae110fc855af906e3da0a92985077fcd488cae4c1c8b5f00e02cf09a","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_3cbd4cb61cbce9dd567e22fa0fc4503d850de2fe561515ce070cbaf7824fbe97","overall_assessment":"The paper provides a specific ethical justification for its use of animal data by referencing the 3Rs principles and includes a statement condemning dual-use for weapons. However, the supplied text does not contain explicit documentation of IRB/IACUC approval, specific data licensing terms, or a formal broader-impact checklist. The evidence is insufficient to determine full compliance with specific venue policies regarding anonymity or plagiarism.","paper_id":"lVmIjQiJJSr","paper_identity_sha256":"692a96b84f90c6821ac2eb6d904e1e309bd66149ae884f167884ffb027965c27","prompt_identity_sha256":"a91cbac4e6d59215e899609a3f6349e834979b51eb38bfc558a195a2ab8e28f9","raw_response_sha256":"f9ab6306202479e712f00f6d251b2289fb40e8cdfbeccca98b5be942a8ce1210","request_identity_sha256":"effdaaa97f5f420a7107ee1cf1b64d0471af435dbc7764ba88032c29e2f83409","reviewer_identity_sha256":"32b29c26fbf1508e066dfb25b1a9a3fe0654c5869a7da3020e1e8e61940befe3","role":"POL","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v4","structural_context_sha256":"acc674ae1538ba3be68faf4b169292ff81cde1149e4513857d9559277cb1cfe9","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-034"],"review_text":"The authors address ethical considerations in the Discussion section by explicitly linking their method to the 3Rs (Replacement, Reduction, and Refinement) for animal ethics. They argue that by improving the detection of subtle biological signals, the method may reduce the number of animals required for specific hypotheses. Additionally, the authors include a statement condemning the use of the RAVE method for weapons or warlike applications. The paper does not discuss potential biases in the data or fairness issues, which is consistent with the specific domain of systems neuroscience where such concerns are less prominent than in social or medical AI.","subdimension_id":"POL-ETH"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-013","SRC-034"],"review_text":"The study utilizes two datasets of two-photon imaging recordings from mouse retinal bipolar cells. The paper states that the code toolbox will be made available as Open Source upon publication. However, the provided text does not specify the licensing terms for the datasets or the code, nor does it explicitly detail the consent or approval processes for the animal experiments beyond the general ethical justification. The data appears to be derived from previously published studies (citations [2] and [39]), but the specific permissions for reuse are not documented in the visible text.","subdimension_id":"POL-DAT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-001"],"review_text":"The paper is submitted under the title 'Anonymous Author(s)' with placeholders for Affiliation, Address, and email. This format is consistent with double-blind review requirements. No author names, institutional affiliations, or self-identifying URLs are visible in the provided text. The evidence is sufficient to confirm that the visible text does not contain obvious anonymity violations, though a full compliance check would require the complete submission package.","subdimension_id":"POL-ANO"},{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The supplied evidence does not contain information regarding plagiarism, self-plagiarism, or dual submission. The paper cites relevant prior work in systems neuroscience and single-cell genomics, but without access to external plagiarism databases or the submission history, it is not possible to verify the originality of the content or the absence of concurrent submissions. The absence of evidence in the text does not prove the absence of misconduct.","subdimension_id":"POL-PLG"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-034"],"review_text":"The paper includes a brief discussion of the broader impact of the work, specifically focusing on the ethical contribution to animal research via the 3Rs and a statement against dual-use for weapons. However, the text does not include a formal broader-impact statement or checklist as often required by modern conference policies. It also lacks explicit documentation of IRB or IACUC approval numbers. The evidence is insufficient to determine if the paper meets all specific policy obligations for broader impact documentation.","subdimension_id":"POL-IMP"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"39f05e735206b739e96c016b9731592d7acb088f587692f1c0af705802d094ac","paper_id":"lVmIjQiJJSr","paper_ordinal":115,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"f9ab6306202479e712f00f6d251b2289fb40e8cdfbeccca98b5be942a8ce1210","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"lVmIjQiJJSr","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"08c0bc8c4c86cfde7c771f435c0cfe571bb4fa4f48511eb4decda6dc6973ca74","request_identity_sha256":"effdaaa97f5f420a7107ee1cf1b64d0471af435dbc7764ba88032c29e2f83409","role":"POL","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v6","usage":{"completion_tokens":830,"prompt_tokens":18699,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_tokens":19529},"valid":true}],"request_identity_sha256":"effdaaa97f5f420a7107ee1cf1b64d0471af435dbc7764ba88032c29e2f83409","role":"POL","role_ordinal":4,"schema_version":"corpus-build-bootstrap-checkpoint-v4"}